#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f0b176c-c802-5b3b-85d0-dede602c9bf3" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Systems of Linear Differential Equations With Complex Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8205f54f-ad97-5a24-9411-ae21ce217e4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164415} {:answer/id #uuid "b6087f3c-2fd7-5bd9-9fb9-38cd74efaaaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164416} {:answer/id #uuid "0d4a6165-100c-5243-918d-0d8fea593f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d4a6165-100c-5243-918d-0d8fea593f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164417} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6458111-ab5c-5d8c-aa47-984f30c58ae0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164414} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29e23fb8-c1d1-5a5e-9a01-11ea7a080d79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381910} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e1cdac-7b2e-5f82-913e-754390960033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381911} {:answer/id #uuid "ab2f15d8-137e-5dae-bbbd-ea6e3c401852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381912} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf42a73-9785-5d3d-aaca-b58afd8101c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381913} {:answer/id #uuid "594d78df-b32e-5382-b242-5df9e09f71e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381914} {:answer/id #uuid "0d8f7109-274d-59bc-8720-4717bdd9949e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d8f7109-274d-59bc-8720-4717bdd9949e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381915} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d0b049d-b68e-502e-a989-9e7aad596a89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09a5051d-6218-52fc-9de8-8eb98b5a1f5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-332952" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=9x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =1\\pm 6\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=1>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b542bd66-f4f8-5b4e-a3e7-4717827c427a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parameters of a System Given Its Phase Portrait"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f90db81d-0268-52f6-b23c-2fc9c698cf75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unbounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381918} {:answer/id #uuid "073b71f8-7c65-52bd-965e-5cbaefe4b927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "073b71f8-7c65-52bd-965e-5cbaefe4b927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381919} :answer-field/id #uuid "df85c79d-21f7-5844-9b5f-3cb7ee09c9bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381917} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a71d392e-23d5-5db8-b506-948d878a78c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381921} {:answer/id #uuid "adc4a9ff-f09f-5dd8-ad20-0924edde8ab1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a71d392e-23d5-5db8-b506-948d878a78c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381921} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2b81281-96e8-5249-9a26-27854a639cfd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :a